<header class="ref-head"><span class="hero-ornament"></span><h1 class="research-title">7 March in history</h1><p class="ref-lede">7 events that happened on 7 March, from 161 to 1965.</p></header>
<ol class="day-events"><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">161 CE <span class="tih-ago">1,865 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Marcus Aurelius becomes Roman Emperor</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">On the death of Antoninus Pius, Marcus Aurelius succeeded and made his adoptive brother Lucius Verus co-emperor. A Stoic philosopher, he wrote his 'Meditations' while campaigning on the Danube.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/danube">Danube</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1799 CE <span class="tih-ago">227 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Napoleon storms Jaffa</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">French troops took the port of Jaffa during Napoleon's Syrian campaign. Thousands of prisoners were then executed, and plague broke out in the army, which was halted at Acre.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/napoleon">Napoleon</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1850 CE <span class="tih-ago">176 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Daniel Webster's 'Seventh of March' speech backs compromise</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">The Massachusetts senator supported Henry Clay's compromise proposals, including a tougher fugitive slave law, to preserve the Union. Many Northern abolitionists denounced him.</p></div></li><li class="tih-event-card tih-has-thumb tih-event-hero"><p class="tih-hero-kicker">&#10022; Anniversary of the day</p><a class="tih-event-thumb" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-graham-bell" tabindex="-1" aria-hidden="true"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/alexander-graham-bell.jpg" alt="" loading="lazy" width="168" height="112"></a><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1876 CE <span class="tih-ago">150 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">Alexander Graham Bell is granted his telephone patent</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">US Patent 174,465 covered a method of transmitting speech electrically. It became one of the most valuable patents ever issued and was defended in hundreds of lawsuits.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag tih-tag-profile" href="/empire/brazilian-empire">Brazilian Empire</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/alexander-graham-bell">Alexander Graham Bell</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1936 CE <span class="tih-ago">90 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">German troops reoccupy the Rhineland</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Hitler sent soldiers into the demilitarised Rhineland in breach of the Versailles and Locarno treaties. France and Britain did not respond with force, encouraging further German expansion.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/versailles">Versailles</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1945 CE <span class="tih-ago">81 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">US troops seize the Remagen bridge over the Rhine</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">American soldiers captured the Ludendorff railway bridge at Remagen before German demolition charges could destroy it. It gave the Allies their first crossing of the Rhine.</p><div class="tih-tags"><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/allies">Allies</a><a class="tih-tag enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/rhine">Rhine</a></div></div></li><li class="tih-event-card"><div class="tih-event-main"><p class="tih-event-year">1965 CE <span class="tih-ago">61 years ago</span></p><h2 class="tih-event-title">'Bloody Sunday' on the Edmund Pettus Bridge in Selma</h2><p class="tih-event-desc">Alabama state troopers attacked about 600 civil rights marchers with clubs and tear gas. Televised images shocked the nation and helped secure the Voting Rights Act that August.</p></div></li></ol>
